# iCloud-fidelity profile "icloud" (scripts/profiles.sh, README.md "iCloud-fidelity profiles").
# Sourced by bash and parsed by scripts/verify-profiles.mjs: plain KEY=value / KEY="value" lines only.
#
# Real iCloud IMAP advertises neither MOVE nor SPECIAL-USE, but does have UIDPLUS and IDLE. So
# imapflow's messageMove() falls back to UID COPY + UID STORE +FLAGS.SILENT (\Deleted) + UID EXPUNGE,
# and special folders are detected by name (specialUseSource "name").
PROFILE_DESCRIPTION="iCloud-like CAPABILITY: no MOVE, no SPECIAL-USE; UIDPLUS and IDLE present"
PROFILE_IMAP_PORT=2143
PROFILE_IMAPS_PORT=2993
# no = drop every special_use line from the template, so LIST carries no \Sent, \Trash, ... attributes.
# (SPECIAL-USE is not advertised either way: with an explicit imap_capability Dovecot adds nothing. With
# yes, LIST would keep the attributes and imapflow would list them in `flags` but still report
# specialUseSource "name", because it trusts attributes only when SPECIAL-USE is advertised.)
PROFILE_SPECIAL_USE=no
# Exact post-login CAPABILITY. Dovecot sends an explicit imap_capability verbatim (it adds nothing), and
# imap-login also uses it for the pre-login list, appending only STARTTLS (port 2143) and AUTH=PLAIN AUTH=LOGIN.
# This is iCloud's published post-login list (MailKit #295, see research-icloud.md section 6) reduced to
# the extensions Dovecot 2.3 actually implements, in iCloud's order. Left out on purpose because Dovecot
# does not implement them: XAPPLEPUSHSERVICE IMAP4 ACL RIGHTS=tekx URLAUTH LANGUAGE CONTEXT=SORT
# METADATA XSENDER X-SUN-SORT ANNOTATE-EXPERIMENT-1 X-UNAUTHENTICATE X-SUN-IMAP XUM1.
# Dovecot extras the main instance has but iCloud does not advertise are also gone: MOVE SPECIAL-USE
# LIST-EXTENDED LIST-STATUS STATUS=SIZE MULTIAPPEND NOTIFY PREVIEW SNIPPET SAVEDATE I18NLEVEL ...
PROFILE_CAPABILITY="IMAP4rev1 QUOTA LITERAL+ NAMESPACE UIDPLUS CHILDREN BINARY UNSELECT SORT CATENATE ESEARCH ESORT THREAD=ORDEREDSUBJECT THREAD=REFERENCES CONDSTORE ENABLE QRESYNC CONTEXT=SEARCH WITHIN SASL-IR SEARCHRES ID IDLE"
